From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ilya Vysotsky <il.mohoff2016@yandex.ru>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 19:38:46 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] Windows 10 Mobile: a read-only region that opens for writing
 is accepted

On a phone unlocked with Interop Tools and vcReg (a Lumia 950 XL) the
system lets a section handle made without write access be duplicated with
it, so PlatformSharedMemoryRegion::Take found every read-only region
writable, and the CHECK in Take ended every start at the first renderer's
shared regions (TransferSharedLastForegroundTime). The guarantee guards a
process boundary this single-process browser has not got: browser and
renderer share one address space, where the region is mapped writable
anyway. Under VENETIUM_W10M such a region is accepted, and the log says so
once; a writable region that cannot be written is still an error.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../platform_shared_memory_region_win.cc      | 19 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 19 insertions(+)

diff --git a/base/memory/platform_shared_memory_region_win.cc b/base/memory/platform_shared_memory_region_win.cc
index 5ee0aa41c28513058e25609ff46640980075ff2b..c614a1edca6e3c81c55069b35154bfc3d2316358 100644
--- a/base/memory/platform_shared_memory_region_win.cc
+++ b/base/memory/platform_shared_memory_region_win.cc
@@ -8,6 +8,7 @@
 #include <stddef.h>
 #include <stdint.h>
 
+#include <atomic>
 #include <string_view>
 
 #include "base/bits.h"
@@ -361,6 +362,24 @@ PlatformSharedMemoryRegion::CheckPlatformHandlePermissionsCorrespondToMode(
   bool is_read_only = !success;
   bool expected_read_only = mode == Mode::kReadOnly;
 
+#if defined(VENETIUM_W10M)
+  // Windows 10 Mobile: on a phone unlocked with Interop Tools and vcReg the
+  // system lets a handle made without write access be duplicated with it, so
+  // every read-only region looks writable here, and the first renderer's
+  // shared regions ended every start. The read-only guarantee guards a
+  // process boundary this browser has not got: browser and renderer are one
+  // process, where the region is mapped writable anyway. Accepted, said once.
+  // A writable region that cannot be written stays an error.
+  if (expected_read_only && !is_read_only) {
+    static std::atomic<bool> said{false};
+    if (!said.exchange(true)) {
+      LOG(WARNING) << "W10M: read-only shared memory can be opened for "
+                      "writing on this phone; accepted (one process)";
+    }
+    return ok();
+  }
+#endif
+
   if (win::GetVersion() >= win::Version::WIN8_1 && is_read_only != expected_read_only) {
     return unexpected(expected_read_only ? TakeError::kExpectedReadOnlyButNot
                                          : TakeError::kExpectedWritableButNot);
